That's exactly the problem with it, it's not that hard to get to the
75% level but because of the absolute reliance on the pet and the easy
death possibilities it's pretty much impossible to make it a really
high-percentage strategy.

> > However a person who has never
> > finished sokoban or been to the bottom of the mines is not a person to
> > suggest such an option to as the difficulty of the game is not quite
> > known yet to them

It's best used by newer players and pacifists--for the newer players
(even those who may have ascended a few times but haven't gotten
comfortable with alternatives to combat), it's not as a high-percentage
ascension strategy but as an impetus for learning non-combat techniques
and once they've successfully pulled it off a few times they can go
back to the safer play but have a new arsenal of tactics in their book.

But I actually _would_ recommend trying it a few times to brand-new
players who rarely reach Soko/Minetown; even if they don't do it
successfully, they'll learn a lot in the process.

Just don't fall in love with it, learn the lessons and then switch to
sounder long-term practices.

> Also if you start with sleep spell and have some food, you can try
